    title: "White House bars CNN from travelling with Trump on Air Force One",
    summary: "CNN was scheduled to fly with US President Donald Trump for his trip to Tennessee on Saturday.",
    preview: "US broadcaster CNN has been barred from travelling with President Donald Trump on Air Force One for a trip to Tennessee on Saturday. The move is the latest in a battle between the White House and the media after it was forced to lift its ban on some news outlets. CNN was scheduled to fly with Trump for his trip to Tennessee for a college American football game until a note released on Friday night by the White House did not list the broadcaster on the media schedule. The BBC has requested comment from the White House.",
    body: "US broadcaster CNN has been barred from travelling with President Donald Trump on Air Force One for a trip to Tennessee on Saturday.\n\nThe move is the latest in a battle between the White House and the media after it was forced to lift its ban on some news outlets.\n\nCNN was scheduled to fly with Trump for his trip to Tennessee for a college American football game until a note released on Friday night by the White House did not list the broadcaster on the media schedule.\n\nThe BBC has requested comment from the White House.\n\nCNN has reported that no other outlet was listed as replacing them in the president's tentative schedule.\n\nLast week Trump banned CNN, Politico and MS NOW journalists from the White House after accusing them of writing \"fiction or lies\" about his administration.\n\nAll three media outlets said they were pursuing legal action, and accused Trump of violating their constitutional rights to free speech and freedom of the press.\n\nFour television networks that have a daily rotation of White House coverage along with CNN - ABC, CBS, Fox News and NBC - had paused their broadcasts of the president in solidarity with the banned outlets.\n\nThe White House then launched its own streaming channel, Trump TV, ahead of the United General Assembly in New York.\n\nA federal judge has since ruled Trump barring news outlets from the White House was likely unconstitutional and the administration had to let them back in, at least for now.\n\nHowever, the White House still denied entry to some CNN and MS NOW reporters assigned to cover arrivals for a state dinner for Chinese leader Xi Jinping on Thursday.\n\nA White House communications account earlier posted on X that \"contrary to what the Fake News wants you to believe, they don't just get to have free rein into every part of the White House, every event, and every press call\".\n\nRegular US television coverage resumed on Friday after White House officials allowed reporters entry.\n\nThe president is set to attend a football game between University of Tennessee vs University of Texas College at Neyland Stadium in Knoxville from midday on Saturday.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Published18 hours ago",
