    summary: "The BBC’s China correspondent Laura Bicker unpacks how the trip panned out for Beijing and Washington.",
    preview: "The worlds two most powerful men just met. How did it go? The worlds two most powerful men â Xi Jinping and Donald Trump â have just met in Washington after days of pomp and pageantry. While there were many symbolic gestures, including Chinese pandas from President Xi, there were few big movements â although they committed to a two month extension of the tariff truce. The BBCs China correspondent Laura Bicker unpacks how the trip panned out for Beijing and Washington.",
    body: "The worlds two most powerful men just met. How did it go?\n\nThe worlds two most powerful men â Xi Jinping and Donald Trump â have just met in Washington after days of pomp and pageantry.\n\nWhile there were many symbolic gestures, including Chinese pandas from President Xi, there were few big movements â although they committed to a two month extension of the tariff truce.\n\nThe BBCs China correspondent Laura Bicker unpacks how the trip panned out for Beijing and Washington.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- China-US relationsUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- United StatesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Xi JinpingUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- ChinaUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
